Frequently asked questions
What is the difference between EHS and EHSQ?
EHS covers environment, health and safety. EHSQ adds quality management, including process consistency, nonconformities and corrective action. Connecting these disciplines can help teams investigate shared operational weaknesses.

Can AI predict every port incident?
No. AI can highlight patterns and potential concerns in available data, but incomplete records, changing conditions and unusual events limit prediction. Competent judgement and effective physical controls remain necessary.

Does a port need cameras and IoT sensors to begin?
No. A port can begin by improving inspections, permits, incident reporting and action tracking. Camera and sensor integrations can be considered where they address a defined need and their performance can be validated.

Can EHSQ software guarantee compliance?
No. Software can help organise obligations, records and follow-up. Compliance depends on applicable requirements, correct implementation and actual operating practices.

How should a port evaluate NeoEHS?
Ask for a demonstration using representative workflows and sample records. Review the required modules, approval rules, access controls, reporting, integrations and implementation support against the port’s needs.

